# Dev folders (NEVER PUBLISH - development artifacts only)
# Wildcard pattern catches all: docs_dev, scripts_dev, tests_dev, samples_dev,
# examples_dev, downloads_dev, libs_dev, builds_dev, etc.
*_dev/

# Agent/script reports — ALWAYS gitignored since they often contain private data
# (full paths, source snippets, API output, validation results, env metadata).
# Canonical rule (~/.claude/rules/agent-reports-location.md): every
# agent/skill/script that saves a report MUST write under the main-repo
# `./reports/<component>/<YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS±HHMM>-<slug>.md`. Neither
# `reports/` nor `reports_dev/` may ever be tracked. `reports_dev/` is
# separately also matched by the `*_dev/` rule above, but it's listed
# explicitly here because the rule says both entries must be present.
reports/
reports_dev/

# Internal review reports (e.g. /review-loop-opus output). Same rationale as
# reports/: they contain absolute paths, internal notes, and per-session
# scratch — never publish them.
reviews/

# Cisco AI Defense skill-scanner runtime artifact (full plugin scan output;
# token-heavy and project-private)
.cpv-cisco-scan.json

# ai-maestro-janitor runtime state (per-machine: heartbeat timestamps,
# safe-delete logs, dedupe seen-files). Never source.
.janitor/

# Trashcan — janitor-safe-delete moves removed items here.
# The dated batch dirs are ignored, but .gitkeep + README.txt are
# tracked so the trashcan survives `git clean -fdx` and fresh clones.
# (The actual /.trashcan/* + negation rules live near the bottom of
# this file — added by safe-delete.sh on first use.)

# Node
node_modules/

# Rust
target/
Cargo.lock
.rechecker/
# TLDR artifacts (added by rechecker)
.tldr_session_*
# Rechecker merge-pending notification files
rck-*-merge-pending.md
/.trashcan/*
!/.trashcan/.gitkeep
!/.trashcan/README.txt

# gh CLI per-host state directory created when running gh inside this repo.
.local/

# cpv-doctor state directory — close-on-publish queue, pending-fix tracking,
# etc. Gitignored: contains issue-number + repo-slug pairs for the doctor's
# fix-and-close-on-publish flow (#8 in the post-diagnosis follow-up menu).
.cpv-doctor/

# Serena MCP server — per-machine project config and cache. Never source.
.serena/

# Issue #33 calibration fixture — a shallow git clone of
# Emasoft/ai-maestro-janitor@v0.5.0 used by tests/test_issue_33_fp_calibration.py.
# Reproducible via the docstring at the top of that test file. Not
# committed to keep the CPV repo size reasonable.
/tests/fixtures/issue_33_no_fp_janitor/

# CI-generated artifacts written into the repo root by .github/workflows/release.yml.
# The Release workflow captures `validate_plugin.py . --strict` output to
# validation-report.txt and copies CHANGELOG.md to changelog.txt, both uploaded
# as release assets. They MUST be gitignored: (1) they're generated, never source;
# (2) the validator's own gitignore-aware tree walk then skips validation-report.txt,
# so its captured output can't trip the encoding control-character check on itself.
/validation-report.txt
/changelog.txt
# NOTE: `reports/` and `reports_dev/` are intentionally NOT repeated here — the
# canonical, commented entries live above (see the "Agent/script reports" block).
# The unanchored `reports/` / `reports_dev/` rules already match the repo-root
# directories *and* any nested copy, so anchored `/reports/` duplicates added
# nothing and were removed to keep a single source of truth.
